ea (PTRO) posted a massive increase in net profit for the first half of 2026 and announced the completion of its purchase of Sejahtera Terminal Logistik (STL). Net profit rose to USD10.78 million, up 913% year‑on‑year, with revenue climbing to USD543.98 million, a 59.55% increase, while equity grew to USD321.28 million and liabilities fell to USD1.20 billion. The acquisition, filed on 15 September 2026, was executed through PTRO’s subsidiaries Petrosea Engineering Procurement Construction and Rekakarsa Karya Nusantara for a total price of Rp880 million, giving Petrosea Engineering 99.80% of STL’s shares (1,497 shares) and Rekakarsa Karya 0.20% (3 shares). The deal is intended to strengthen PTRO’s logistics and port‑service operations and generate synergies.', '5325', null, '109.682066506209', '12.0698882349974', '9.369735053243044', '4.148290172966714', '14836185595140', '482143939680', '10.8352317228066', '1.2993746081929', '-14.152615285002538', '3.894804476403275', 'lebih mahal/berisiko', 'netral', 'di atas sektor', 'wajar', '{"peers":[{"peers_data":{"companies":[{"year":2025,"group":["self"],"pb_mrq":11.5032268155139,"pe_ttm":104.532673712491,"symbol":"PTRO.JK","market_cap":51186703750000,"net_income":482143939680,"company_name":"Petrosea Tbk","employee_num":4031,"total_assets":26491858014180,"total_equity":5145758518680,"pretax_income":657374675880,"total_revenue":14836185595140,"point_summaries":[{"name":"value","point":6,"maxpoint":18},{"name":"competitive","point":19,"maxpoint":25.5},{"name":"future","point":0,"maxpoint":6},{"name":"financials","point":3,"maxpoint":7.5},{"name":"dividend","point":1.5,"maxpoint":11},{"updatedAt":"2026-09-15T23:01:12.632Z"}],"yearly_mcap_chg":0.371621621621622,"operating_expense":749073740220,"revenue_breakdown":null,"total_liabilities":21346099495500,"int_income_breakdown":null,"operating_expense_breakdown":null},{"year":2025,"group":["sub_sector","sector","industry","sub_industry"],"pb_mrq":1.85949038348108,"pe_ttm":3.350609