-5a8780e1f222', '71ca3d88-32c0-406d-9a03-1ae7e9a7074d', 'BYAN.JK', 'Bayan Resources Tbk', 'energy', 'RKAB signal completed, PT Bayan Resources Tbk (BYAN) surges 19.96% to Auto Reject Top (ARA) in Session I', ARRAY['Market Sentiment','Mergers & Acquisitions','Ownership','Bullish'], 'PT Bayan Resources Tbk (BYAN) jumped 19.96% to reach the Auto Reject Top (ARA) level in the first session of trading on 18 September 2026 after the RKAB signal was completed. The stock opened at Rp13,825, rose 2,300 rupiah, with a volume of 8.88 million shares traded in 4,909 transactions for a total value of Rp122.66 muliar, while the broader IHSG fell 0.28% to 6,444. The rally followed BYAN’s disclosure that founder Low Tuck Kwong and his daughter Elaine Low signed a Conditional Share Purchase Agreement on 16 September 2026 with PT Jhonlin Baratama, which will acquire 10,000,000,500 ordinary shares, roughly 30% of BYAN, and PT Jhonlin Baratama is part of Jhonlin Group. Earlier, BYAN announced force majeure for its subsidiaries Tiwa Abadi (TA), Tanur Jaya (TJ) and Fajar Sakti Prima (FSP) pending the revision of their 2026 RKAB, a process the Ministry’s Dirjen Minerba expects to complete within the week.', '11525', null, '27.1256908210475', '8.64844914850338', '28.498478171928937', '0.25252880900422353', '57365496738143', '12852187283440', '10.8352317228066', '1.2993746081929', '15.494951548263735', '0.9122250458919005', 'lebih mahal/berisiko', 'netral', 'di atas sektor', 'wajar', '{"peers":[{"peers_data":{"companies":[{"year":2025,"group":["self"],"pb_mrq":8.51712779483847,"pe_ttm":26.7138039756086,"symbol":"BYAN.JK","market_cap":378333352250000,"net_income":12852187283440,"company_name":"Bayan Resources Tbk","employee_num":3384,"total_assets":56486296335228,"total_equity":45097802085795,"pretax_income":16937619897693,"total_revenue":57365496738143,"point_summaries":[{"name":"value","point":7,"maxpoint":18},{"name":"competitive","point":19.5,"maxpoint":25.5},{"name":"future","point":0,"m